WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.440
Surrounded at Gaixia, Xiang Yu knew the situation was desperate, and sat alone in his tent.

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:08.510
Outside the tent, the Han army's encirclement grew ever tighter.

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:13.372
He drank wine and sang, lamenting his strength and his fate — a heroic, sorrowful song.

00:00:13.722 --> 00:00:17.682
He raised his cup and drank it down, his eyes full of sorrow.

00:00:18.032 --> 00:00:23.120
The beautiful Consort Yu stayed beside him, dancing softly with a sword, tears glistening.

00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:28.222
The sword light flashed, as if bidding Xiang Yu a final farewell.

00:00:28.572 --> 00:00:32.580
This was their last time together; outside the tent lay endless night and the enemy army.

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:36.602
The two held close to each other, treasuring these final moments.

00:00:36.952 --> 00:00:43.192
The story of the Hegemon-King's farewell has been handed down through the ages, becoming one of the most moving chapters in literature and opera.

00:00:43.542 --> 00:00:48.462
On the opera stage, performers have acted out this story again and again.

00:00:48.812 --> 00:00:54.044
By the Wu River, the morning mist slowly lifted, and the water flowed quietly on.

00:00:54.394 --> 00:00:57.706
People remember this hero — and they remember the couple's story too.

